            "wizardHelp": {
                "message": {
                    "copyInputFields": [
                        {
                            "description": "Use the following URL as a <strong>Redirect URI</strong> of the Incode onboarding client.",
                            "value": "registration_redirect_uri"
                        },
                        {
                            "description": "Use the following URL as a <strong>Redirect URI</strong> of the Incode face authentication client.",
                            "value": "redirect_uri"
                        },
                        {
                            "description": "If the face authentication client is used for password recovery, also add the following <strong>Redirect URI</strong>.",
                            "value": "recovery_redirect_uri"
                        }
                    ],
                    "header": "Prerequisites",
                    "paragraphs": [
                        "Create one connection per Incode client: one for the <strong>onboarding</strong> client (used in self-registration and invited-user registration) and one for the <strong>face authentication</strong> client (used in login and password recovery).",
                        "Register <Code class=\"inline-code\">https://&lt;host&gt;/accounts/register</Code> on the onboarding client, and <Code class=\"inline-code\">https://&lt;host&gt;/commonauth</Code> and <Code class=\"inline-code\">https://&lt;host&gt;/accounts/recovery</Code> on the face authentication client in the Incode Dashboard.",
                        "The local attributes <Code class=\"inline-code\">incodeIdentityId</Code>, <Code class=\"inline-code\">incodeInterviewId</Code> and <Code class=\"inline-code\">incodeOnboardingStatus</Code> must exist: the connection maps the Incode claims to them. Also add the OpenID Connect attribute <Code class=\"inline-code\">identity_id</Code> mapped to <Code class=\"inline-code\">incodeIdentityId</Code>: the account is linked to it.",
                        "In a self-registration flow, the Incode step can be placed before or after the form that asks for the username and password: a username chosen in the form is kept.",
                        "In a login flow, add the Incode step after the step that identifies the user, such as <strong>Username &amp; Password</strong>, and keep that step as the subject identifier step. The connector sends the identity linked to the user as <Code class=\"inline-code\">login_hint</Code>. In a password recovery flow, add the Incode step with the face authentication connection after the step that identifies the user."
                    ],
                    "link": {
                        "text": "See Incode's guide on OIDC clients.",
                        "url": "https://developer.incode.com/concepts-and-architecture/oidc-manual-configuration/"
                    }
                },
                "fields": [
                    {
                        "fieldName": "Name",
                        "hint": "A unique name, e.g. Incode Onboarding or Incode Face."
                    },
                    {
                        "fieldName": "Client ID",
                        "hint": "The <Code class=\"inline-code\">Client ID</Code> of the Incode OIDC client."
                    },
                    {
                        "fieldName": "Client secret",
                        "hint": "The <Code class=\"inline-code\">Client secret</Code> of the Incode OIDC client."
                    },
                    {
                        "fieldName": "Authorization Endpoint URL",
                        "hint": "Incode authorization endpoint of your environment."
                    },
                    {
                        "fieldName": "Token Endpoint URL",
                        "hint": "Incode token endpoint of your environment."
                    }
                ]
            }
        },
